WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.280
Review with the other model before you ship.

2
00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:07.550
Claude Code finished this task on a branch.

3
00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:11.972
specweave review --brief shows what a reviewer gets:

4
00:00:11.972 --> 00:00:14.130
who wrote the code, from the ledger,

5
00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:17.870
the acceptance criteria, and the diff since the branch began.

6
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.030
Before you ship, run specweave review.

7
00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:24.807
Claude wrote the code, so it picks Codex, from another family.

8
00:00:24.807 --> 00:00:28.058
Codex gets the brief in a read-only sandbox.

9
00:00:28.058 --> 00:00:30.345
This run took about 30 seconds.

10
00:00:30.345 --> 00:00:34.340
Its verdict is fix first, so the command exits 3.

11
00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:38.583
The review is saved in reports/review-codex.md.

12
00:00:38.583 --> 00:00:42.504
Each finding cites a file and line, and how to fix it.

13
00:00:42.504 --> 00:00:47.340
Here, a blank name gets no fallback, which breaks AC-02.

14
00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:51.839
Claude's fix trims the name, and falls back to world when it's empty.

15
00:00:51.839 --> 00:00:54.933
It also adds a test for blank names.

16
00:00:54.933 --> 00:00:57.490
Run the tests: all three pass.

17
00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:01.049
Then run specweave review again, on the fixed code.

18
00:01:01.049 --> 00:01:05.491
No critical or high finding is left, so the verdict is ship,

19
00:01:05.491 --> 00:01:07.320
and the exit code is 0.

20
00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:11.726
Each run adds a note to the ledger, with the reviewer and its verdict.

21
00:01:11.726 --> 00:01:15.905
Both notes name the same file, and the second run overwrote it:

22
00:01:15.905 --> 00:01:19.720
the fix-first report is gone, so keep a copy if you need it.

23
00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:23.880
specweave pickup shows the latest notes to whoever comes next.

24
00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:26.753
Next, run specweave verify,

25
00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:30.330
then close the increment with specweave complete.
